  "notes": "Hand-transcribed 2026-10-02 from the official Butler University Department of Arts Administration (Jordan College of the Arts) 'Bachelor of Science (BS) in Arts Administration - Music - Summary of Degree Requirements' (Spring 2026 version). Suggested Sequence of Courses transcribed verbatim; semester totals match the PDF's stated totals (15/17/15/15/15/13/15/15 = 120 across 8 semesters). Repeated enrollments: Major Instrument or Voice applied study (AM __, 4 semesters) x 2 credits = 8; Major Ensemble (ES __) 7 semesters x 1 = 7; allow_repeated_courses is set and documented here. Studio Class (AM 222, 226, or 298, 0 credits) is taken each semester of applied study if required by the applied teacher. Music History electives (9 credits): choose three of MH 305, MH 306, MH 307, MH 308-SJD, MH 408-ICR. Arts Administration electives (6 credits): choose two of AA 315, 330, 335, 383, 390, 425, 450. Experiential Learning: AA 371-ICR (1 cr), AA 372-ICR (2 cr), and/or AA 373-ICR (3 credits total). Internship Preparation (AA 400) is 0 credits; Internship in Arts Administration (AA 475) is 6 credits. Arts Administration majors fulfill the Social World core (9 social-science credits), Perspectives in the Creative Arts, ICR, and BCR. JCA Talent Award footnote: recipients must take applied lessons at the major level and participate in a major ensemble every semester on campus. For students considering professional music careers or graduate music study, adding the BA in Music as a secondary major (17 additional music credits) is recommended. Prerequisites are not listed in the summary; prereq arrays are empty (chains live in the Bulletin course descriptions).",
